<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/400546522%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Son Espases Roman Camp";
    rdfs:comment "This Roman camp, discovered in northern Palma, Mallorca, during construction of the Hospital de Son Espases, dates to Metellus' conquest of the island ca. 123-121 BCE. The visible remains on the north side of the hospital were consolidated and moved from the larger site, which is no longer visible.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/400546522> .

