<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/40080%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Berenice Panchrysos";
    rdfs:comment "Berenice Panchrysos was a settlement in the Eastern Desert of Egypt. It was located near Sabae in the Regio Troglodytica (modern Sudan). Its name (\"all golden\") derives from its proximity to the gold mines Jebel Allaqi (Jebel Ollaki) that were exploited in antiquity.";
