<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413025/bacucco> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The Barrington Atlas Directory and several antiquarian sources link this toponym to Aquae Passeris. This place does not appear in modern gazetteers, however, so the possibility must be entertained that this locality (località) is now superseded or outmoded. George Dennis includes this place name in his 1848 \"The Cities and Cemeteries of Etruria\", noting that Bacucco is found \"Five miles north of Viterbo, on the left of the road to Monte Fiascone\" and that the ruins there may correspond to Aquae Passeris. Based on the attestation in the Barrington Atlas Directory, the temporal attestation is recorded as the 20th century.";
    dcterms:modified "2026-04-16T15:39:29-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Bacucco";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413025/bacucco> .

