<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413079%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Le Ciliegeta";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/676201591%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The site of Le Ciliegeta, near the source of the river Arno, served as a rich stips votiva. The site was discovered in 1836. The finds included over 600 bronzes, more than 1,000 pieces of aes rude, 2,000 weapons, and other artifacts.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413079> .

