<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413302%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "S. Valentino";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/991900272%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Remains of at least two Roman villas have been identified in the frazione of San Valentino, part of the larger comune of Poggio Mirteto. One is the so-called Villa dei Casoni, while this site is sometimes known as the Bagni di Lucilla. This villa was the findspot in 1801 of a mosaic pavement now in the Chiaramonti museums of the Vatican.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413302> .

