<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/418515134%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Koyuk Shahri";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient fortified site known as either Koyuk Shahri or Kuiyukexiehai'er that is located in the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region of north-western China preserves evidence of urban occupation in the Tarim Basin during the first millennium BCE. The site consists of a walled area of some 60,000 m² with an artificial mound at the center of the walled space.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/418515134> .

