<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/420811320%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Wadi al-Jarf";
    rdfs:comment "Site on the Red Sea Coast in Egypt, used in the Fourth Dynasty as a port for importing turquoise and copper from Sinai. The oldest surviving papyrus from Egypt, dated during the reign of Khufu (26th century BCE), was found at the site.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/420811320> .

