<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/420860522%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Zalu Ab";
    rdfs:comment "Zalu Ab (also Romanized as Zālū Āb and Zālūāb) is a village in Zalu Ab Rural District, in the Central District of Ravansar County, Kermanshah Province, Iran. Several ancient objects, including a bronze bowl of a Chaldean tribal leader, are reported to have been discovered in this rural Iranian village.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/420860522> .

