<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422836%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Antemnae";
    rdfs:comment "Antemnae is an ancient Latin settlement located north of Rome near the point where the Anio and Tiber rivers intersect. Connected with Rome's early history, Antemnae was involved in episodes such as the 'Rape of the Sabine Women' and Romulus is said to have celebrated a triumph over the Antemnates in 752 BC.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422836> .

