<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422850%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Il Barco";
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Barco Borghese\" is an archaeological site located in Monte Porzio Catone (Roma) in Italy. This multiperiod site began as a Roman terracing or substructure, perhaps originally meant to support a villa (basis villae). Subsequent modification and reuse converted the Roman structure into a \"barco\", an enclosure for animal hunts.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422850> .

