<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422898%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Collatia";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/272213280%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Collatia was an ancient city of Latium located between Gabii and the Anio River. A colony of Alba Longa, Collatia was one of the most ancient cities of Latium. Subjugated by Rome under the Tarquins, Collatia would decline during the Republican period and numbers among the lost Latin cities by the accounting of Pliny the Elder.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422898> .

