<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422928%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Fosso della Crescenza";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/774612717%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/963165127%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "John Ward-Perkins identified the archaeological site at Fosso della Crescenza during the South Etruria Survey. Excavations of a Iulio-Claudian mausoleum were undertaken in 1962. Additional excavation revealed portions of the Via Veientana. Post-excavation work did not occur until the 1980s, by which time Fentress 1983 notes that the archaeological landscape had been largely eradicated by the burgeoning growth of suburban Rome.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422928> .

