<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422939%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Grotta Papale";
    rdfs:comment "The site of a Roman villa situated on two terraces. The modern toponym \"Grotta Papale\" derives from a partially subterranean apsidal nymphaeum. The villa was extensive, covering some 23,000 square meters and has both a late republican and an imperial phase.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422939> .

