<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422953%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ladispoli";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/190306780%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/346600104%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/506528154%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/533417134%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/584868519%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Ladispoli is a modern toponym; it is a comune of the Metropolitan City of Rome and is situated 35 kilometers (22 miles) west of Rome, on the Mediterranean Sea coast. In terms of the ancient landscape, present-day Ladispoli lies in the environs of ancient Alsium. Based on archaeological remains, Ladispoli was a popular locus for coastal villas.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422953> .

