<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423004%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Plinio";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/835948519%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called villa of Pliny the Younger, also known as the Villa della Palombara. The villa's first phases date to the Iulio-Claudian period. It continues in use, and continues to undergo modifications, through the second century A.D.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423004> .

