    rdfs:comment "The Villa Muti in Grottaferrata occupies, at least in part, the site of a Roman republican villa built on a series of terraces and likely dating to the third and second centuries B.C. Lanciani excavated a series of rooms at the site. The site also had an early to mid-Imperial phase that included elaborate floors and decoration in imported marble.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423130> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423130/osm-location-of-villa-muti> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "Representative location of the modern villa grounds on which ancient remains are evident based on a way derived from OpenStreetMap";
    dcterms:modified "2024-09-08T10:52:57-04:00";
    dcterms:title "OSM location of Villa Muti";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423130/osm-location-of-villa-muti> .

