<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/459721458%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Pompey";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/109182%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Pompey (Meurthe-et-Moselle, France) produced archaeological evidence of a Roman productive site located near the junction of the Meurthe and Moselle rivers. This site was discovered in 1962 and has been described as a \"villa rustica\". There is evidence of baths and painted wall plaster. There is evidence for pottery production at the site, along with agricultural activity. There is a cremation necropolis of the second and third centuries CE described as containing \"poor\" finds.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/459721458> .

