<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/475092090%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Oviedo";
    rdfs:comment "Founded in the eighth century, Oviedo was modeled after Toledo and flourished in the ninth century under Asturian King Alfonso II (791-842). It was at that time that Oviedo became the Asturian capital and an episcopal see. Oviedo remained prominent until the early tenth century.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/475092090> .

