<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/477295678%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple at Santa Maria in Canale";
    rdfs:comment "A temple of Tuscan type with cella and lateral alae built of ashlar masonry and dated to the 3rd century BCE, now built into a rural church and farmstead complex. The temple is situated along the Via Amerina between Ameria and Tuder, and marks the boundary between those two Umbrian communities. A fragmentary Umbrian bronze inscription (Vetter 229) of around 300 BCE mentioning a deity characterized as \"Iovia\" was discovered here in the 18th century CE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/477295678> .

