<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/494566507%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Habuba Kabira (South)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912849%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/923122730%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The southernmost of two associated settlements located on the western bank of the Euphrates, and one of the only examples of large-scale residential architecture from the Late Uruk period. Rescue excavations were conducted at the site before it was inundated by the Tabqa Dam Reservoir in the early 1970s.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/494566507> .

