    rdfs:label "Shamiram Canal";
    rdfs:comment "The \"Shamiram canal\", also referred to as the \"Semiramis canal\", is located to the east of Van, Turkey, and runs for some 45 miles to Lake Van. On the basis of epigraphic evidence, its original construction is attributed to King Menua of Urartu.";
