<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/49850%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Alagankulam";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/50737%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The ancient settlement associated with the modern village of Alagankulam on the Vaigai river in Tamil Nadu is thought to have been an ancient seaport though now positioned some 3 kilometers from the coast. The immediate area has produced local and imported ceramics (including Mediterranean amphorae and Roman potsherds), as well as fourth-century Roman coins.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/49850> .

