<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/404426272%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433032%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/599902893%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus (Regio VII, Insula 16, entrances 12-15) is considered to be the residence and trading center of the gens Umbricia, a Pompeian family involved in producing and selling garum. The house itself is described as a \"Samnite-type\" house and in the first century B.C. it was most likely owned by the Samnite military commander Maras Spurnius who resisted the invasion of Sulla.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/404426272> .

