<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413124%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Faesulae";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/394362505%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/488345053%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/587811162%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Faesulae (modern Fiesole) was an Etruscan foundation called Viesul, Viśl, or Vipsul. The city was conquered by Romans in 283 B.C. Sulla would settle Roman veterans there. Citizens of the town supported the conspiracy of Catiline.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413124> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413127%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Falerio";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/262385625%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413341%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/672180338%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/67911853%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Falerio was the site of a substantial ancient settlement on the left bank of the river Tinna. Under Augustus, a colony of veterans assigned to the tribus Velina was established there.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413127> .

