<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413352%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Trevignano";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413290%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Trevignano Romano, located on the shores of Lake Bracciano, lies some 47 km from Rome. Archaeological evidence for Etruscan occupation, in the form of tombs dating to the eighth - sixth centuries B.C., has been discovered to the north of the modern town. A medieval castle was built there under Innocent III ca. 1200.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413352> .

