    dcterms:description "The so-called \"Barco Borghese\" is an archaeological site located in Monte Porzio Catone (Roma) in Italy. This multiperiod site began as a Roman terracing or substructure, perhaps originally meant to support a villa (basis villae). Subsequent modification and reuse converted the Roman structure into a \"barco\", an enclosure for animal hunts.";
