        <http://viaf.org/viaf/46755947>;
    dcterms:description "Ladispoli is a modern toponym; it is a comune of the Metropolitan City of Rome and is situated 35 kilometers (22 miles) west of Rome, on the Mediterranean Sea coast. In terms of the ancient landscape, present-day Ladispoli lies in the environs of ancient Alsium. Based on archaeological remains, Ladispoli was a popular locus for coastal villas.";
