        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/297163721%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/441989089%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/743823049%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An ancient settlement on the right bank of the river Astura, Satricum has a mixed heritage of Latins and Volscians. In 499 B.C. Satricum was a member of the Latin League, but was under Volscian control in 488 B.C. The site is noted for its sanctuary of Mater Matuta.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423060> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423061%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Saxa Rubra";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422941%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/856514595%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Saxa Rubra (modern Grottarossa) is the name of a road station on the Via Flaminia, nine Roman miles from the center of ancient Rome. It was at Saxa Rubra that Constantine I defeated Maxentius in A.D. 312.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423061> .

