    rdfs:label "Agnone";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432838%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Agnone is a comune in the Italian province of Isernia, in the Molise region. It lies about 53 km (33 miles) northwest of Campobasso. An ancient center of Oscan-Samnite culture, Agnone is known particularly as the namesake of the third-century BCE \"Agnone tablet\" that was discovered at Fonte di Romito.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432656> .

