<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432782%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Circeii 1";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/328868135%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432783%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Circeii received a Latin colony ca. 390 B.C. The remains on the site include an enclosure wall built in polygonal masonry. \"Circeii 1\" refers to the earlier Roman colony founded at the eastern side of Monte Circeo. The settlement eventually moved to the western side of the peninsula.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432782> .

