    rdfs:label "Damecuta";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432752%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An Imperial villa excavated by A. Maiuri in the 1930s, Damecuta was connected to the Iulio-Claudian emperors. The construction of later Medieval and Bourbon fortifications on the site significantly damaged the ancient remains. The Medieval Damecuta tower stands atop part of the Roman villa.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432811> .

