<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433024%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Picentinus Ager";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433199%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/544710173%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Picentinus Ager is an area of Campania in the valley of the river known in present-day terms as the Picentino. Pliny the Elder claims that this territory was originally occupied by the Etruscans; in 268 BCE, the Roman state resettled the Picenes there. This occasioned the foundation of a settlement called Picentia. While the location of that settlement remains uncertain, the archaeology of Pontecagnano shows a long, continuing arc of human activity from the Iron Age to the Roman period.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433024> .

