<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/444064177%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Pranu Muttedu";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472014%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Pranu Muttedu is a pre- and protohistoric archaeological site located near Goni, Sardinia. The complex includes standing stones (menhirs) and prehistoric built tombs (domus de janas). The site dates to the Late Neolithic (3200 – 2800 BC) and Early Chalcolithic (2800 – 2600 BC) periods.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/444064177> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/44420465> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Apollod. Bibl. (Frazer: Perseus) 1.6.3",
        "Elton 2004 ",
        "MANTO 9055591: the Corycian Cave (Cilicia)",
        "Mela (Ranstrand: PHI) 1.72-75",
        "Str. (Meineke: Perseus) 9.3.1";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ghawes>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rselth>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rssmith>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "A large karstic grotto and cave, known today as Cennet ve Cehennem, which is located about 7km from Corycus in Cilicia. It was described by Mela, Apollodorus, and Strabo and was associated with the Titan Python in Greek mythology. It is not to be confused with the well-known Corycian Cave on mount Parnassos in Greece.";
