    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "ATAE Assur 52b (Egyptian Archive) ",
        "Miglus, Radner and Stępniowski 2016 121–126",
        "Pedersén 1998 143";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ptushingham>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/tseidler>;
    dcterms:description "In a fill from private house in Room 1A2 (in area eA8V), excavators discovered an archive of 15 texts, belonging to a group of Egyptians. Some of these people have Egyptian names, others have Assyrian names. Available datings belong to a period of some 30 years in the mid-7th century BC. The archive consists of legal documents.";
