<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/459049147%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Lacus Curtius";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/502866838%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Lacus Curtius is an area in medio foro connected with the earliest phases of Rome's occupation. By the late Republican period, it had become a small basin set inside a paved area. Livy relates the famous episode of the Sabine Mettius Curtius in relation to his description of the site.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/459049147> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/459128239> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Wikipedia (Turkish) Dilkaya Höyüğü";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "An ancient tell located approximately 24 km from the city center of Van. Dilkaya Höyüğü is located just west of Dilkaya Village in the southwest of the Edremit district. It lies on the northern side of Hoşap Stream, on the shores of Lake Van.";
