        "PECS (Perseus) POMPEY Meurthe-et-Moselle, France",
        "vici.org 66988: Pompey";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "Pompey (Meurthe-et-Moselle, France) produced archaeological evidence of a Roman productive site located near the junction of the Meurthe and Moselle rivers. This site was discovered in 1962 and has been described as a \"villa rustica\". There is evidence of baths and painted wall plaster. There is evidence for pottery production at the site, along with agricultural activity. There is a cremation necropolis of the second and third centuries CE described as containing \"poor\" finds.";
    dcterms:modified "2026-06-12T11:21:27-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Pompey";
