    rdfs:comment "In the modern province of Catania, the site of Castiglione di Ragusa is on a hilltop some 7 km northwest of Ragusa. Already inhabited in the Early Bronze Age, the hill was occupied by a Sikel settlement from approximately the seventh to fifth centuries B.C., with subsequent occupation in the fourth and third centuries B.C.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462144> .

