<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462159%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Chrysas, T.";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "According to Cicero, the shrine of Chrysas (the god shares a name with the nearby river) was located along the road from Assorus to Henna. A cult image in marble, described as being \"beautiful\", was to be found there and was ultimately spared from the depredations of Caius Verres.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462159> .

