<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472526695%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Roman Mausoleum of Villa Gordiani";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422936%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Roman Mausoleum of Villa Gordiani is a two-storey cylindrical tomb with pronaos executed in opus latericium. It fronts on the ancient via Praenestina. The rotunda has a diameter of more than 19 meters. Based on brick stamps, chronology is potentially wide and likely should be assigned anywhere in the period from Constantine I to Theodoric.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472526695> .

