<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472637%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Decimomannu Roman bridge";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472014%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The remains of a stone, arched Roman bridge at Decimomannu, to the west of Assemini, Sardinia. Three of the original six arches survive today. The bridge may originally have been as much as 160 meters in length. R.J. Rowland considered it to be of Iulio-Claudian date.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/472637> .

