    dcterms:coverage "Alagankulam";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/erdosy-m-u>;
    dcterms:description "The ancient settlement associated with the modern village of Alagankulam on the Vaigai river in Tamil Nadu is thought to have been an ancient seaport though now positioned some 3 kilometers from the coast. The immediate area has produced local and imported ceramics (including Mediterranean amphorae and Roman potsherds), as well as fourth-century Roman coins.";
