    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "AD79 Reg VII, Ins 16",
        "Arachne BT4649: Atrium 2 der Casa VII 16, 12-15 - Casa di A. Umbricius Scaurus Pompei",
        "Jashemski 2002 439",
        "PompeiiinPictures VII.16.15 Pompeii. Casa di Umbricius Scaurus (I) or House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus, Father and Son (I)",
        "Wikidata House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus (Q27688002)";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus (Regio VII, Insula 16, entrances 12-15) is considered to be the residence and trading center of the gens Umbricia, a Pompeian family involved in producing and selling garum. The house itself is described as a \"Samnite-type\" house and in the first century B.C. it was most likely owned by the Samnite military commander Maras Spurnius who resisted the invasion of Sulla.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-04-07T12:10:13-04:00";
    dcterms:title "House of Aulus Umbricius Scaurus";
    cito:citesAsRelated <http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/bauwerksteil/4649>,
