    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Arachne sog. Palazzo Imperiale sog. Palazzo Imperiale, Ostia",
        "Ostia - Harbour City of Ancient Rome Regio I - Palazzo Imperiale (Imperial Palace)",
        "Spurza 1999 ";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The so-called Palazzo Imperiale at Ostia is located at the western margin of Regio I. This building complex was initially excavated between 1855 and 1871 and many of its finds, especially mosaics, were transported to the Vatican Museum. The complex dates to the second and third centuries CE and includes a variety of installations - shops, storehouses, bathing facilities - but is most likely not a palace despite its modern sobriquet.";
