        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/580975875%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/674520031%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Ferentium (modern Ferento) was a city of Etruria first mentioned in the Liber Coloniarum ca. 123 BC that became a Roman municipium after the Social War. Substantial remains of the city remain; the site was the birthplace of Otho and is noted for its fine stone monuments and statues.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413132> .

