    dcterms:coverage "Palestrina";
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/12320449>,
        <http://viaf.org/viaf/46755947>;
    dcterms:description "An ancient city of central Italy, the eighth and seventh century B.C. origins of which demonstrate high-level trade contact with the Eastern Mediterranean world. The city withdrew from the Latin League (499 B.C.) and opposed Rome in the Latin war; Cincinnatus eventually subdued Praeneste. Sulla founded a new colony there in the first century B.C.";
