<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423117%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Velitrae";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422991%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433208%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/745915669%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Velitrae (modern Velletri) was an ancient Volscian settlement. In the Roman Republican period, Velitrae was attacked by Marcus Furius Camillus (379 B.C.) and again by Cincinnatus (377 B.C.); the Romans controlled the site by 365 B.C. The gens Octavia hailed from the city and a youthful Octavian spent time there.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423117> .

