    rdfs:comment "The Lucus Furrinae or Syrian Sanctuary is a sanctuary site on the Janiculum Hill in Rome. The first known construction at the site took place during the late first century CE, and it remained in use until the mid-fourth century CE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432336962> .

