        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/24617478>;
    dcterms:description "Picentinus Ager is an area of Campania in the valley of the river known in present-day terms as the Picentino. Pliny the Elder claims that this territory was originally occupied by the Etruscans; in 268 BCE, the Roman state resettled the Picenes there. This occasioned the foundation of a settlement called Picentia. While the location of that settlement remains uncertain, the archaeology of Pontecagnano shows a long, continuing arc of human activity from the Iron Age to the Roman period.";
