<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/443954%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ponte S. Venere";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/356966898%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/442485%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/442727%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A much-repaired medieval bridge crossing the Aufidus (modern Ofanto) river. Long a traditional candidate location for the \"Pons Aufidi\" shown on the Peutinger map (thus BAtlas), recent survey work has found no evidence in the area consistent with a Roman-era bridge. The Pietra Dell'Oglio bridge (further south on the Ofanto) is of Roman date and now a more likely candidate. The Ponte S. Venere remains in use today for the Strada Statale 303.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/443954> .

