    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462459%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An ancient settlement of Sicily mentioned by Ptolemy and by Procopius. It has been long identified by many scholars with an archaeologically attested settlement at modern Punta Secca; however, identification has been rejected, because there is no natural harbor at Punta Secca, by RJA Wilson in favor of an as-yet-unlocated position on the coast somewhere east of Capo Scalambri.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/465930> .

