<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/408534260> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Richardson 1992 243, 246";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "A place included in the Regionary Catalogues for Regio XI, the Aedes Mater Deum is otherwise obscure. According to Richardson, the toponym may refer to the statue of Magna Mater on the spina of the Circus Maximus.";
