    rdfs:comment "Centum Cellae (modern Civitavecchia) was an ancient coastal settlement in Tyrrhenian Etruria. The emperor Trajan rebuilt the harbor at the site in 106/7 and Pliny the Younger mentions its name, Centum Cellae. Saracens destroyed the city in A.D. 812.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413076> .

