    dcterms:coverage "Ponte S. Venere, over R. Ofanto at Pons Aufidi on Via Appia";
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/71459378>,
        <http://viaf.org/viaf/76387372>;
    dcterms:description "A much-repaired medieval bridge crossing the Aufidus (modern Ofanto) river. Long a traditional candidate location for the \"Pons Aufidi\" shown on the Peutinger map (thus BAtlas), recent survey work has found no evidence in the area consistent with a Roman-era bridge. The Pietra Dell'Oglio bridge (further south on the Ofanto) is of Roman date and now a more likely candidate. The Ponte S. Venere remains in use today for the Strada Statale 303.";
    dcterms:modified "2023-10-14T16:10:52-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Ponte S. Venere";
