    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/wilson-r-j-a>;
    dcterms:description "Archaeological area near Sortino, in Sicily, famous for its large rocky necropolis. The place was occupied from the 13th century BC to the Byzantine period. Formerly identified with the ancient settlement of Herbessos, it is now more often associated with Hybla Gereatis.";
