    rdfs:comment "A Hernican hill town that formed part of a sixth-century B.C. defensive league against Volscian and Samnite aggression and allied itself to Tarquinius Superbus. Rome eventually took Aletrium in 306 B.C.; by the first century B.C., the town was a Roman municipium.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432664> .

