    rdfs:comment "An ancient Roman road branching off from the Via Flaminia and continuing to Luna, where it joined the Via Aurelia. The Via Cassia post-dates the Via Amerina and was built after 240 B.C. It combined new construction with re-use of pre-existing roads and tracks.";
